# A collection export is personal data — which cards this machine's Arena account
# owns — and this repository is public. The file is committed empty so that its
# presence is documented rather than mysterious, and a clean filter guarantees it
# stays that way: `git add` runs the working copy through `true`, which produces
# nothing, so whatever is in the working tree never reaches a commit.
#
# The filter needs one local setting, because git does not take a filter command
# from a repository (that would let a clone run arbitrary code):
#
#   git config filter.strip-collection.clean true
#
# Without it the file is committed verbatim, so CONTRIBUTING lists it in setup.
/collection.txt filter=strip-collection
